description:
12+12+12 month contract - 40 hours per week
Baseline Security Clearance Required
QLD, WA, ACT, VIC, NSW, NT, SA or TAS (hybrid / WFH)
Work within the Biosecurity & exports domain
Our client, a large Federal Government Department, who enhance agriculture industries, forestry, trade and biosecurity require the services of a Azure Data Engineer. 
Duties of the Azure Data Engineer
Design, develop and maintain data pipelines using Azure-native services (e.g. Azure Data Factory, Fabric, SQL, storage services);
Build & manage ELT patterns using code-first approaches;
Optimise queries, pipelines & data models for performance & cost efficiency;
Implement automated data quality checks & validation rules;
Monitor pipelines & troubleshoot production issues;
Improve observability & operational resilience of data assets; &
Work with analysts, data scientists, architects and business stakeholders to translate requirements into effective technical solutions.
 Skills and Experience Required
Extensive experience designing, building & maintaining robust, production‑grade data pipelines using code‑first ELT patterns;
Advanced SQL capability, including complex transformations, optimisation & performance tuning on large datasets;
Proven experience designing and operating data pipelines using cloud‑native services;
Tertiary qualification in IT, Computer Science, Data, Engineering or a related discipline, related certifications, or equivalent experience (desired);
Demonstrable knowledge of Azure ecosystem with relation to data management ecosystem (desired);
Demonstrable knowledge of SQL, Python, Pyspark, or other programming languages for data management (desired); &
Understanding access control, appropriate data handling, & risk considerations for sensitive or regulated data (desired).
How to Apply 
For a copy of the full job description, including the application instructions, please get in touch with Ben at Recruitment Hive by clicking the Quick Apply button. Alternatively you can reach Ben on (02) 6299 1*** to discuss further. 
Please note that applications close on Friday the 15th of May 2026 at 11am. 
Recruitment Hive welcome late applications to be considered for future opportunities. 
Job ID: BC670580 | LH-06453
  We Value Diversity 
The Recruitment Hive is a proud Equal Opportunity Employer. We recognise the value of diverse perspectives and experience and are committed to an inclusive workplace where everyone feels valued and respected for who they are. We encourage people with disability, indigenous, veterans and people of all backgrounds and abilities to express their interest in this role.
